# ---- Data ------------------------------------------------------------
# The raw dataset and every derived split are large and regenerable
# (source/preprocessing/pipeline.py). Ignored by extension rather than by
# directory so a future data/processed_<variant>/ needs no new rule, and so
# the small JSON sidecars beside them stay tracked -- feature_columns.json
# is read at serve time and COPYd by the Dockerfile, so a fresh clone must
# have it.
data/**/*.parquet
data/**/*.csv
data/**/*.db
data/*.db

# ...except the Mininet-demo dataset: 254 flows, ~150KB total (splits + the
# raw labelled CSV). Small, not regenerable without the VM, and the paired
# artifacts/models/mininet-demo model was trained on exactly these splits.
!data/mininet_demo/**

# ...and the GNS3 integration-test dataset: captured on the real-OS (Alpine)
# GNS3 topology, ~200KB, paired with artifacts/models/gns3-demo. Same reason
# as above -- not regenerable without the GNS3 lab.
!data/gns3_demo/**

# Window-size / feature sweeps: many variants of the same split (~1.7GB),
# none of them needed to reproduce the deployed model.
data/processed_experiments/

Dataset/data/*.csv

# ---- Artifacts -------------------------------------------------------
# Ignore generated model/data files by extension rather than blanket-ignoring
# the directory -- `artifacts/*` would also hide artifacts/models/README.md
# (hand-written, meant to be tracked) since git won't look inside an ignored
# directory at all, no matter what's negated below it. Extension-based
# matching also scales to any future artifacts/models/<version>/ folder.
artifacts/**/*.pkl
artifacts/**/*.pt
artifacts/**/*.json
artifacts/**/*.csv

# ...except the deployed model and the preprocessing artifacts paired with
# it. The Dockerfile COPYs both, so a clone missing them cannot build or
# serve -- and model.pt is the deliverable. ~276KB together, which is what
# a version-controlled artifact this small should cost.
!artifacts/models/optuna-denoising-50/**
!artifacts/preprocessing_w50/**

# ...and the Mininet-demo model (documentation/guides/mininet-live-demo.md):
# the network-specific autoencoder that turns the NF-ToN-IoT-v2 AUROC 0.000
# into 0.998. Same small footprint, and the live demo cannot be reproduced
# without it, its preprocessing artifacts, and the tiny captured dataset below.
!artifacts/models/mininet-demo/**
!artifacts/preprocessing_mininet/**

# ...and the GNS3-demo model + preprocessing: the autoencoder retrained on the
# GNS3 topology for the integration test (network_simulation/gns3/). Paired
# with data/gns3_demo above; same small footprint, not regenerable without the
# lab.
!artifacts/models/gns3-demo/**
!artifacts/preprocessing_gns3/**

# ...and the resource benchmark, which is a measurement rather than a
# generated model file. The rule above is about not versioning large
# derived artifacts; this is 6KB of results that a report cites.
!artifacts/benchmark.json
!artifacts/benchmark-constrained.json
!artifacts/explanation-evaluation.json
!artifacts/protocol-thresholds.json

# ---- Python ----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- Virtual environments --------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---- Editors / OS ----------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# ---- Misc ------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
